Z||000005||mrfiero||11-22-2000||02:14 AM||||If we're only talking chassis, then two.  The main location at the base of the windshield and under the dash on the drivers side (on frame rail).  I have heard that there is another one somewhere, but I haven't found it (haven't really looked). <P>If you include all of those paper tags, then the number grows to 6 or 7.  I have found them under the speedo surround, under the front dash speakers, under the radio surround, under the carpets, and once under the shifter surround (could have slipped in there).<P>Am I missing any place?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 11-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||11-22-2000||12:22 PM||||The paper tags are on the fenders, on the front fascia in the center up against the front cross support, rear fascia behind the licence plate.  Must be on the doors someplace and other panels.||||reg||3
Z||000007||mrfiero||11-22-2000||01:19 PM||||Well he said excluding the body panels, so I did not count those.....only '87 & '88 models have the tags on the body panels anyways.<P>The paper tags I am talking about are found in the interior of all Fieros. ||||reg||1
